<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Only Latin-script locales are declared. The active keyboard renders QWERTY, AZERTY
  and QWERTZ letter layouts with locale-specific long-press accents and offline word
  lists. Declaring Arabic, Devanagari, CJK, Cyrillic, Greek or Hebrew subtypes without
  a matching layout/composition path was misleading: a 50-word lexicon is not a layout.
  All declared subtypes are ASCII capable, so Android can offer them in ASCII-only
  editors (password, URI, email) instead of silently skipping the keyboard.
-->
